CantonLink Community Dictionary data
====================================

The dictionary dataset in this folder is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

You may copy, share and adapt it, including commercially, provided that you
credit the sources below, say if you made changes, and share your version under
the same licence.

The dataset is built from open sources. It must carry these credits:

- CC-Canto and the CC-CEDICT Cantonese readings: copyright (c) 2015-2017
  Pleco Software Incorporated, under CC BY-SA 3.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/). CC BY-SA 3.0 allows
  adaptations to be shared under a later version of the same licence, which is
  why the combined dataset is offered under CC BY-SA 4.0.
  Source: https://cantonese.org/download.html
- CC-CEDICT: the CC-CEDICT contributors, published by MDBG under CC BY-SA 4.0.
  CC-CEDICT contains portions of the original CEDICT database, copyright (c)
  1997, 1998 Paul Andrew Denisowski.
  Source: https://www.mdbg.net/chinese/dictionary?page=cc-cedict
- Tatoeba: example sentences and their translations are contributed by Tatoeba
  users and released under CC BY 2.0 FR
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/). Each example keeps its
  Tatoeba sentence id so it can be traced to its contributors.
  Source: https://tatoeba.org
- HKCanCor, the Hong Kong Cantonese Corpus, compiled by Kang Kwong Luke and
  May L.Y. Wong, under CC BY 4.0. It is used only to count word frequency.
  Cite: K. K. Luke and M. L. Y. Wong (2015), The Hong Kong Cantonese Corpus:
  Design and Uses, Journal of Chinese Linguistics Monograph Series, 25, 312-333.

CantonLink's own corrections (corrections.json) and generated fields (Yale,
Bopomofo, ranking) are offered under the same CC BY-SA 4.0 licence.

Every entry is external and unreviewed. No entry has been checked by native
speakers for CantonLink.

How the source files and their licences were checked is recorded in
SOURCES.md.
